tests/ui/check/err_uncertainty_operands.sky:2:9: error: an uncertainty cannot be negative
  |
2 | a = 5 ± -0.1
  |         ^^^^ this is negative
  = note: `±` takes a standard uncertainty, which is never negative
  = help: write its magnitude: `x ± 0.1`

tests/ui/check/err_uncertainty_operands.sky:3:12: error: `±` needs scalar operands
  |
3 | b = [1, 2] ± 0.1
  |            ^
  |     ------ this is Vector[2] [1]
  |              --- this is Scalar [1]
  = note: arrays cannot carry an uncertainty yet
  = help: write `±` on each element you need

tests/ui/check/err_uncertainty_operands.sky:4:5: error: `±` needs a number, found Bool
  |
4 | f = true ± 1
  |     ^^^^ this is Bool
  = note: v0.1 has no truthiness: a Bool is never a number

tests/ui/check/err_uncertainty_operands.sky:5:5: error: `nominal` takes 1 argument, found 2
  |
5 | d = nominal(1, 2)
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ wrong number of arguments
  = help: call it as `nominal(x)`

tests/ui/check/err_uncertainty_operands.sky:6:17: error: `uncertainty` takes a scalar, found an array
  |
6 | e = uncertainty([1, 2])
  |                 ^^^^^^ this is Vector[2] [1]
  = note: arrays cannot carry an uncertainty yet
